---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Plain-language terms of use. Kept short and consistent with EDITORIAL.md:
// the record links to its sources, other outlets are attributed,
// and corrections are visible. The effective date is the date of the last
// substantive edit.
const EFFECTIVE = "November 10, 2026";
---

<Base
	title="Terms of use — Chino Valley Today"
	description="The terms for using Chino Valley Today: what the site is, what it promises, and what it does not."
>
	<header class="legalhead">
		<div class="shell legalhead__inner">
			<h1 class="legalhead__title">Terms of use</h1>
			<p class="legalhead__date mark">Effective {EFFECTIVE}</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<div class="reading body prose">
		<p>
			These terms apply to chinovalley.today and its feeds. By using the site
			you agree to them. If anything in them is unclear, email
			<a href="mailto:corrections@chinovalley.today"
				>corrections@chinovalley.today</a
			>.
		</p>

		<h2>What the site is</h2>
		<p>
			Chino Valley Today is an independent local news site. It reports what
			public bodies in Chino and Chino Hills did, assembled from their public
			records with automated checks and human review, as described on the
			<a href="/about/">About</a> page. It is not affiliated with the City of
			Chino, the City of Chino Hills, the Chino Valley Unified School District,
			or any agency it covers.
		</p>

		<h2>The record is the authority</h2>
		<p>
			Civic claims on the site link to the record they came from. We work to
			get each one right and we correct mistakes visibly, but the site is
			provided as is, without warranties of any kind, express or implied.
			Where this site and the primary record disagree, the primary record
			controls. Nothing here is legal or other professional advice. Do not
			rely on the site alone for legal, financial, safety, or
			deadline-sensitive decisions; follow the link and confirm with the
			agency. During an emergency, follow official alerts and instructions.
		</p>

		<h2>Other people's content</h2>
		<p>
			Headlines and short summaries from other news outlets are attributed to
			them and link to their articles; those articles belong to their
			publishers. We feature a story to point readers to it. Featuring it
			does not endorse it, and what another outlet says is its statement, not
			ours.
		</p>
		<p>
			A publisher who wants their work removed from this site can
			email the address above, and we will remove it promptly.
		</p>

		<h2>Using what is here</h2>
		<p>
			You are welcome to read, link to, quote, and share the site's own
			writing, with credit to Chino Valley Today and a link back. Public
			records and archived agency documents remain public records, and we
			claim no ownership of them. Please do not republish the site in bulk or
			present it as your own.
		</p>
		<p>
			Automated access is welcome within reason: use the
			<a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> where you can, identify your client
			honestly, and keep request rates modest. Do not attempt to disrupt the
			site or get around its security.
		</p>

		<h2>Corrections</h2>
		<p>
			If something here is wrong, tell us. Corrections are made openly: the
			original text stays, struck through, with a dated note. See
			<a href="/about/">About</a> for how corrections are handled.
		</p>

		<h2>Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains what the site
			collects.
		</p>

		<h2>Liability</h2>
		<p>
			To the extent the law allows, Chino Valley Today and the people who run
			it are not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of the
			site, your reliance on it, or the sites and services it links to.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes and governing law</h2>
		<p>
			These terms may change, and the effective date at the top will change
			with them. Using the site after a change means you accept the updated
			terms. These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.legalhead {
		background: var(--crate);
		color: #fff;
		border-bottom: 6px solid var(--placard);
	}
	.legalhead__inner {
		padding-block: 1.9rem 2.2rem;
		max-width: 44rem;
	}
	.legalhead__title {
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 1.2rem + 2vw, 2.5rem);
		line-height: 1.16;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.legalhead__date {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
	}
	.body {
		padding-block: 2.4rem 1rem;
	}
</style>
